# Netlify SPA fallback.
#
# IntruSight is a client-side-routed React application: only index.html exists
# as a real file, and react-router resolves /login, /alerts, /admin/users and
# the rest in the browser. Without this rule Netlify looks for a matching file
# on disk, finds none, and returns its own 404 page for any direct navigation
# or refresh on a nested route — and for the hard redirect the API client
# performs on a 401 (window.location.href = "/login").
#
# Status 200 (a rewrite, not a 302) keeps the requested URL in the address bar
# so react-router sees the original path.
/*    /index.html   200
